  "note": "Triennial election of Belfast Corporation, polled Wednesday 21 May 1958: 90 candidates for 53 seats (45 councillors and the aldermen of eight wards); contests in 13 of the 15 wards (Belfast News-Letter, 8 and 9 May 1958). Victoria Ward's councillors were elected on 19 June 1958 (separate folder) after the death of a candidate. Both papers print Boylan 526; the News-Letter's printed majority (581) is reckoned against Carlin's 508 and is not recorded. The Irish News reads Carlin 308 (probably a misprint). Spoiled papers 122 in the councillors' poll (64 in the aldermanic poll)."
